# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Environment variables — copy to .env / .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real keys.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#   .env        → non-secret config. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser
#                 bundle at BUILD time, so they must ALSO be set as build-time env vars on
#                 the host (DigitalOcean App Platform) or the deployed bundle keeps
#                 whatever was baked into the last build.
#   .env.local  → server-only SECRETS. Gitignored. Must stay uncommitted.
#
# ── Supabase ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# The client-safe publishable key (sb_publishable_...). Never the secret key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://portableofficecabin.com

# SERVER-ONLY. Bypasses Row Level Security — treat it like a database root password.
# Put this in .env.local (and in the host's *runtime* secrets), never in .env.
# Required by /api/razorpay/order and /api/razorpay/verify: RLS deliberately gives users
# NO UPDATE on `orders`, so only the server (holding this key) can mark an order paid.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Razorpay ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get these from the Razorpay Dashboard → Settings → API Keys.
# Use rzp_test_* keys until the flow is verified, then swap to rzp_live_*.
#
# SERVER-ONLY (put both in .env.local / host runtime secrets):
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_ID     — the key id. Public-safe in itself, but read on the server and
#                         handed to the browser by /api/razorpay/order, so the checkout
#                         cannot drift from the key that actually created the order.
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET — THE SECRET. Signs and verifies payments. If this leaks, anyone
#                         can forge a "payment verified" signature. Never expose it, never
#                         prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never send it to the browser.
#
# Both API routes fail with an explicit 500 if either is missing — they will not silently
# pretend to take a payment.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxx
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# SERVER-ONLY. A DIFFERENT secret from RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET above — do not reuse that one.
# This is the value you type into the Razorpay Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks when creating
# the webhook; Razorpay signs each delivery's RAW body with it and /api/razorpay/webhook
# verifies that signature before trusting a single byte of the payload.
#
# Required by /api/razorpay/webhook. The webhook is the AUTHORITATIVE record of payment: the
# browser's /verify call can be lost (customer closes the tab the instant payment succeeds),
# but Razorpay guarantees webhook delivery. Without this variable the route returns 500 and
# Razorpay retries — so payments would be taken but orders never marked paid.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# OPTIONAL. The current checkout does NOT need this: it uses the keyId returned at runtime
# by /api/razorpay/order (which avoids the "NEXT_PUBLIC_ was baked into an old build"
# class of deploy bug entirely). Set it only if a client component ever needs the key id
# directly — and if you do, it MUST be identical to RAZORPAY_KEY_ID above.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── AI Construction Animation Builder ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers the concept-animation workspace on
#   /products/home-construction/building-construction-contractor
#
# ALL SERVER-ONLY. None of these carries a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so Next.js will not inline
# them into the browser bundle; every provider call is made from an /api/animation-studio
# route. Put them in .env.local / the host's runtime secrets.
#
# LEAVING THEM UNSET IS A SUPPORTED STATE. With no provider configured the workspace still
# accepts uploads, validates them, analyses (see below), builds and edits the 30-second
# storyboard and saves projects — it simply refuses to start a render and shows a
# "Video provider configuration required" panel naming the variables below. It never
# simulates a successful generation.

# Which adapter to use: "google-veo" or "generic". Omit and it is inferred from whichever
# credential set below is complete.
VIDEO_PROVIDER=google-veo

# --- Google Veo (Gemini API) -----------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY is the name the Gemini API documentation uses, so it is what you will already
# have if you followed those docs. Required for VIDEO_PROVIDER=google-veo.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to veo-3.1-generate-preview. Also accepts veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview.
# Set this to pin or upgrade the model without a code change.
GEMINI_VIDEO_MODEL=
# Optional. Defaults to https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta
GEMINI_API_BASE_URL=
#
# BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY ONLY — do not set these on a new deployment. They were the variable
# names this feature originally shipped with, and are still read when the GEMINI_* names above
# are unset, so an existing deployment keeps working without a rename during a deploy.
# GOOGLE_VEO_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_VEO_MODEL=
# GOOGLE_VEO_BASE_URL=
#
# VEO CLIP LENGTHS ARE DISCRETE: 4, 6 or 8 seconds, and 16:9 or 9:16 only. The storyboard
# requests the next length UP from each scene's slot and ffmpeg trims it back down, which is how
# six scenes of 5/6/5/4/7/3s become a file that measures exactly 30.000s. See
# src/lib/animation/providers/veo.ts and scripts/animation-studio.test.ts section 3b.

# --- Generic REST provider -------------------------------------------------------------
# For any service exposing submit / status / download. Lets a provider be swapped in with
# no adapter written. Required for VIDEO_PROVIDER=generic.
VIDEO_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=
VIDEO_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides — defaults shown in src/lib/animation/env.ts
VIDEO_PROVIDER_SUBMIT_PATH=/v1/videos
VIDEO_PROVIDER_STATUS_PATH=/v1/videos/{id}
VIDEO_PROVIDER_CANCEL_PATH=
VIDEO_PROVIDER_AUTH_HEADER=Authorization
VIDEO_PROVIDER_AUTH_SCHEME=Bearer
VIDEO_PROVIDER_LABEL=
# SERVER-ONLY. HMAC-SHA256 key the provider signs webhook deliveries with. Without it the
# webhook route rejects every request — an unsigned callback must never mark a job complete.
VIDEO_PROVIDER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Image analysis (OPTIONAL) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Vision model used to READ the uploaded exterior/interior images and pre-fill the
# "Locked Building Features" panel. Without it the panel is filled with reference-copying
# defaults marked "not detected" and the UI says so — it never claims a detection that did
# not happen. Falls back to GEMINI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_VEO_API_KEY when unset.
BUILDING_ANALYSIS_API_KEY=
BUILDING_ANALYSIS_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
BUILDING_ANALYSIS_BASE_URL=

# --- Storage + session -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Private Supabase Storage bucket created by
# supabase/migrations/20260824120000_construction_animation_studio.sql
ANIMATION_STUDIO_BUCKET=animation-studio
# SERVER-ONLY. HMAC key signing the anonymous visitor's project-ownership cookie. Falls back
# to SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY if unset; set a dedicated value in production so rotating one
# does not rotate the other. Any long random string (32+ bytes) is fine.
ANIMATION_STUDIO_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Media tooling (OPTIONAL) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute paths to ffmpeg/ffprobe when they are not on PATH. ffmpeg is what joins the scene
# clips into ONE exact-30-second H.264 MP4; without it scenes still render and download
# individually, and the export button explains why it is disabled. ffprobe verifies the
# exported duration — when it is absent the built-in MP4 container reader measures it
# instead (src/lib/animation/probe.ts).
FFMPEG_PATH=
FFPROBE_PATH=

# ── Verifying it all works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Once the key is set, the migration applied and ffmpeg installed, prove the whole pipeline
# end to end (submit → poll → download → assemble → ffprobe → private storage):
#
#   npm run animation:live -- --confirm --scenes=2 --resolution=720p
#
# It SPENDS PROVIDER CREDIT, refuses to run without --confirm, and never prints or stores a key.
# /api/animation-studio/config reports the same readiness as JSON at any time.
